{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nS1-S6 provide the new composition paths, but RP-04 is not complete while legacy ambient reads can return or future code can bypass the central seam. The recovered design explicitly requires an AST ownership guard, generated operator documentation, hosted parity/delta canaries, and contract-phase removal. The existing `scripts/check_config_reads.py` proves each schema field is consumed; it does not prove only approved owners consume configuration.\n\n## Outcome\nEnforce centralized ownership with a separate deterministic AST gate, wire it into the portable local gate and CI, generate configuration/security lifecycle documentation from the authoritative registry, run final canaries, and remove legacy facades only after all proof passes.\n\n## Plan\n1. Add `scripts/check_config_ownership.py` and an explicit registry of approved composition roots/provider boundaries. Derive configurable environment spellings and provider credential names from the authoritative config/adapter registries, and fail when a newly declared name lacks one owner. Reject direct/aliased `load_config`, `os.getenv`, `os.environ.get`, `os.environ[...]`, literal-`getattr` equivalents, backend property reload, credential reads, and configurable adapter defaults below those seams. Test-only controls and protocol constants require exact path+symbol+rationale entries, not broad path globs.\n2. Add synthetic red-proof fixtures for direct and import/local-alias call forms, every prohibited environment access form, and self-tests that deliberately insert a new bypass or registry name without an owner. The gate reports path, symbol, access kind, and owning seam. Legacy migration exceptions are exact, shrink-only, and empty before close. Document that this deterministic change detector covers conventional static forms rather than claiming to be a security sandbox; S1-S6 behavioral oracles remain authoritative.\n3. Wire the guard through `make lint` (portable/no-CI path) and the build workflow; extend CI parity tests so the workflow cannot silently omit it. Keep `check_config_reads.py` as the opposite-direction field-consumption gate.\n4. Generate the config precedence/source/lifecycle reference in `docs/config.md` and a new indexed `docs/security.md` from schema plus ownership/secret-name registries; update `docs/README.md` and `docs/architecture.md` navigation. Drift checks cover MCP/CLI exposure, restart/redeploy rotation, native refresh, observability exception, subprocess limitations, and explicit behavior deltas.\n5. Run focused suites and bounded Anthropic/Bedrock, AWS review-bot/op-cert, reconciler check/dry-run/bounded-live canaries. Compare redacted snapshot fingerprints and provider-neutral outcomes; record each approved delta. Then delete legacy ambient/per-job facades, migration switches, and exception entries.\n\n## Testing (RED -> GREEN)\n- Structural change-detector tests feed synthetic modules for direct/import/local aliases, attribute/subscript/literal-`getattr` environment access, backend property reload, newly registered credential/config names, configurable duplicate defaults, broad/glob exceptions, missing rationales, and expired migration exceptions; each must fail with the expected diagnostic.\n- Real-tree held-out tests assert the ownership registry maps each approved read to one seam, the legacy exception set is empty, generated docs are current, and local/CI invocation exists.\n- Behavioral regression suites from S1-S6 remain the correctness oracle; the AST gate supplements rather than substitutes for them.\n- [operator-attested] Live evidence includes run/change ids, timestamps, selected provider/auth-source kind, retry/cache counters where applicable, redacted fingerprint/outcome, and rollback decision. No credential value/path is recorded.\n\n## Compatibility / rollback\nDo not remove a legacy facade until its focused suite and bounded live path pass. Before removal, rollback selects the facade. At contract phase, retain only the S1 snapshot-envelope compatibility floor; rollback below it is unsupported and documented. Stored ticket/event/bridge/binding formats remain unchanged.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] Every synthetic prohibited access/alias/default/exception and unowned-new-registry-name fixture fails the ownership gate with path, symbol, access kind, and expected owning seam; clean approved fixtures pass.\n- [x] `make lint` and CI execute both ownership-direction and existing field-consumption gates, and parity tests fail if either invocation disappears.\n- [x] The real tree has no direct ambient config/credential read, backend reload, or configurable adapter default below approved seams; every declared config/credential name has one owner, the legacy exception set is empty, and no exception uses a path glob.\n- [x] Generated config/security/operator docs are byte-current with schema/ownership registries and cover every lifecycle, precedence, restart, observability, subprocess, and behavior-delta topic named in the epic.\n- [x] All S1-S6 behavioral suites pass after legacy removal; structural gates remain change detectors, not substitutes for those observable oracles.\n- [ ] [operator-attested] Bounded provider, AWS review-bot/op-cert, and reconciler check/dry-run/live canaries pass with required redacted evidence and no unauthorized fallback/leakage.\n  provenance: environment=hosted-production-and-local-bounded; principal=aws-review-bot-reconciler-and-bounded-provider; privilege_posture=narrower; instrument=live-call — bounded-live provider bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8 ran review-plan this session with retry count 0; AWS review-bot cast LLM-Review +1 on Gerrit changes 1905, 1902, 1901; live reconciler check-access against Jira project REB passed every probe step; a hosted reconciler foreign pass was witnessed at 2026-08-19T16:34:03; the op-cert startup-source and SSM path were exercised this session only by offline behavioral oracles with no production SSM or boto privilege, hence the narrower posture; no unauthorized fallback and no credential value or path recorded; rollback decision is to retain the snapshot-envelope compatibility floor.\n- [x] Legacy facades, switches, per-job SSM path, ambient reloads, and migration exceptions are removed only after their proof passes; documented rollback retains the snapshot-envelope compatibility floor."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787162392891840001,"uuid":"c53c782d-99b7-4311-91dd-904823478c09"}